# Moby Docker SDK CVEs -- both affect Docker plugin installation/AuthZ,
# which the culvert-updater sidecar never uses (it only calls container
# lifecycle APIs: inspect, pull, create, start, stop, remove, logs).
# Accepted under RISK-ACC-1 (docs/engineering/TECHNICAL-RISK-REGISTER.md)
# until the updater module is removed (DEBT-008).
#
# exp: dates are enforced by trivy itself -- once the date passes, the CVE
# stops being ignored and the blocking gate goes red, forcing re-triage
# (RISK-006). If the updater removal slips past the date, re-validate the
# reachability rationale and extend deliberately; do not extend by reflex.
CVE-2026-34040 exp:2026-10-01
CVE-2026-33997 exp:2026-10-01
